we start with breaking news sky news  understands that the whole of  nottinghamshire  will go into tier 3 lockdown on  friday morning nottingham city  brookstowe  gedling and rushcliff council areas had  already been preparing to enter  tier three at midnight tonight instead  the entire county will go into the  highest restrictions  together on friday well let's cross  live to westminster and our political  correspondent kate mccann  uh kate i suppose the government's done  this in order to ease confusion  for those in that part of the world i  think that's been the general aim here  is to make sure that the whole county  goes into the same tier  tier three at the same time and of  course as you said there some areas had  been expecting this perhaps a little  earlier than  friday at midnight but now the whole  county will move into that much more  stricter  lockdown measure together as one and the  local mps have generally welcomed it  there had been some suggestion that  hospitals in nottinghamshire  had had to cancel some cancer operations  and that of course had led to  increased levels of concern about rising  infections in fact the infection rate in  nottinghamshire has  on the whole come down from the peak  where it was around seven days ago but  still  running at quite a high level and some  pretty big concerns about what happens  if it doesn't  go lower than where it is now so clearly  tier three  the most strict tier of the government's  new system  is where ministers feel is appropriate  at the moment that of course means that  people cannot socialize in the ways that  they were before that some places will  be closed pubs and restaurants for  example can't open  unless they're serving a substantial  meal what it will mean for people though  living there  is a big change in their way of life and  of course there is a whole debate now  about how areas can move out of these  tiered systems  and what kind of things the government  is looking at to reduce restrictions on  people's lives  for the moment though at that point in  time the whole of the county of  nottinghamshire will move into tier  three together  at the end of this week
 

